{
  "name": "n8n Form Dynamic Dropdown from Data Table for Stock Requests",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "s2-1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1100,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\n1. **Stock Request Form** (login required) asks for name and email.\n2. **Build Item Page** lists each active, in-stock item as `#id · name · stock` on **Choose Item and Quantity**, a Form page built from JSON on every visit.\n3. **Check Request** re-reads the item by its `#id` and checks the quantity: a whole number from 1 to the stock and `max_quantity_per_request`. Stale or edited choices get the page again with the reason (up to `max_attempts` tries).\n4. **Take Stock** only writes if the stock is unchanged since the check, so the last units cannot be taken twice.\n5. The request is logged; the requester gets a confirmation page and email receipt.\n6. Stock at or below an item's `low_stock_threshold` emails the stock keeper once; `low_alert_sent` blocks repeats until a request finds the item restocked above it.\n\n### Setup\n1. Execute **Run Once to Create Tables** (needs permission to create data tables), then add items with `name`, `unit`, `stock`, `low_stock_threshold` (empty = no alert) and `active` ticked. The workflow fills `low_alert_sent` and `change_token`.\n2. Attach a Basic Auth credential to **Stock Request Form** and an SMTP credential to both email nodes.\n3. In **Stock Request Settings** set `stock_table_name`, `log_table_name`, `stock_keeper_email`, `from_email` (an address your SMTP account may send from), `max_quantity_per_request`, `max_attempts`.\n4. Set the Workflow settings timezone, activate, and share the Production URL of **Stock Request Form**.\n\n### Customization\nUntick `active` to hide an item without deleting it.\n\nLimits: a failed log write still takes the stock (the page says so). A failed alert email clears the flag so the next request retries (unless clearing fails too). Deleting a table mid-request stops that request.",
        "width": 600,
        "height": 1300
      }
    },
